## The shared writing cycle

F01–F06 began as free investigations before a resource pause; their drafts were preserved for continuation. S02 began from the accepted I012 idea packet. Each draft then went to two separate critics, one focused on the argument and one on literature. After both reports were archived, a fresh editor wrote a response and R1.

The critics reviewed the original draft. R1 has not received another independent review, so both versions remain available for comparison. A completed cycle records the work done; the [current selection](../../docs/selection.md) records how the candidates will be used.

Human direction covered process and resources; AI supplied the arguments and revisions. The [research record](../../docs/provenance.md) explains authorship, context separation, and capture coverage. Each biography gives its release time and recorded settings; its metadata preserves exact timestamps, source fingerprints, and the link to the canonical Russian history. [Date policy](../../logs/DATES.md) · [Source index](index.json).
